# AMCP Clients

> Web and desktop client applications for the AI Modular Cybersecurity Platform.

## What lives here

This repository contains the user-facing applications and client-side presentation layer.

Includes:
- web UI
- desktop client
- shared client-side assets if needed
- front-end build and deployment configuration

## Desktop client build notes

The desktop app is a Qt project and is cross-platform in source, but each OS requires its own native build.

### Linux

```bash
cd amcp-platform-clients/apps/desktop-client
cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja
cmake --build build --target amcp_admin_desktop amcp_user_desktop -j$(nproc)
```

Run:

```bash
./build/amcp-admin-desktop/amcp_admin_desktop
./build/amcp-user-desktop/amcp_user_desktop
```

### Windows

Build on Windows or a Windows CI runner using Qt 6 and CMake/Ninja, then deploy with `windeployqt`.

### macOS

Build on macOS or a macOS CI runner using Qt 6 and CMake/Ninja, then deploy with `macdeployqt`.

## Help Docs Source (Supabase)

Help docs for both web and desktop clients are hosted in Supabase Storage.

- Source files are in `docs/help/`.
- A manifest file (`docs/help/manifest.json`) defines doc metadata.
- Both clients fetch this manifest and open the docs from the public bucket path.

### Sync docs to Supabase

Run from this repository root:

```bash
SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co \
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service-role-key> \
HELP_DOCS_SUPABASE_BUCKET=client-docs \
HELP_DOCS_SUPABASE_PREFIX=help \
node scripts/sync-help-docs-to-supabase.mjs
```

The script uploads `manifest.json` and all `.md` docs from `docs/help/`.
It also creates the storage bucket as public when it does not exist.

## Repository layout

```text
amcp-platform-clients/
├── apps/
│   ├── desktop-client/
│   └── web-client/
└── README.md
```

## How to use it

1. Keep all user-facing applications here.
2. Talk only to stable APIs, SDKs, or events.
3. Do not depend on internal service or training code.

